            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "107\t\n108\t\\emph{Threshold sensitivity.}\n109\t$\\Kempirical$ depends on the operational threshold $\\theta$.\n110\t$\\Kempirical \\geq 2$ across $\\theta \\in \\{0.55, 0.60, 0.65\\}$ for all four decoding strategies, rising to $\\Kempirical = 3$ at $\\theta = 0.55$ (all four 2v3 $\\auc$ values exceed 0.55) and returning to $\\Kempirical = 2$ at $\\theta \\in \\{0.60, 0.65\\}$; at $\\theta = 0.70$, $\\Kempirical = 1$ for all model-mode configurations.\n111\tBeyond decoding parameters, the threshold sensitivity extends to generation mode: at $\\theta{=}0.65$, continuation-mode configurations drop to $\\Kempirical{=}1$, while rewrite mode retains $\\Kempirical{=}2$.\n112\tOur current analysis primarily covers the decoding configuration axis."
            }
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "session": "worker_writing_fix-reviewer-info-residual_20260514T054533",
